###############################################
# NOTES AND GUIDELINES
###############################################

# 1. Replace {{baseUrl}} with your actual API base URL (default: http://localhost:3001)
# 2. Replace {{accessToken}} with actual JWT token from login response
# 3. Replace {{refreshToken}} with refresh token from login response
# 4. Replace IDs ({{userId}}, {{vehicleId}}, etc.) with actual IDs from database
# 5. Use HTTP Client extension in VS Code to execute these requests
# 6. All timestamps should be in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ)
# 7. Status codes:
#    - 200 OK: Successful GET, PATCH, DELETE
#    - 201 Created: Successful POST
#    - 400 Bad Request: Invalid input data
#    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid token
#    - 403 Forbidden: Insufficient permissions
#    - 404 Not Found: Resource not found
#    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error
# 8. Test sequence recommendation:
#    1. Register/Login
#    2. Create resources (vehicles, branches)
#    3. Create bookings
#    4. Create payments
#    5. Create support tickets
#    6. View analytics

###############################################
# END OF TEST SUITE
